  "notes": "B.S. Fashion Merchandising. Built from the official Kent State University program page 'Plan of Study Grid' (http://www.kent.edu/fashion/fashion-merchandising-bs), which mirrors the University Catalog. Students must declare and graduate with a minor (any Kent State minor); minor requirements are modeled as generic elective slots. A study abroad/away experience is required (minimum 2.500 overall GPA to participate). Third Summer Term: FDM 45192 Internship in Fashion Merchandising (ELR), 3 credits; minimum 2.500 overall GPA required for the internship. Prerequisite chain follows the course sequence: FDM 10033/10034 Fashion Fabrics -> FDM 20030 Fashion Apparel Analysis; FDM 20263 Fashion Retail Industry -> FDM 30262 Fashion Merchandise Planning and Buying -> FDM 40262 Data-Based Decision-Making; MATH 10041 -> FDM 30270 Trends and Predictive Analytics; FDM 30083 Professional Seminar -> FDM 40270 Fashion Industry Research Methods (WIC); FDM 30260 -> FDM 40299 Applied Principles (capstone ELR).",
